      en: ["Zakučac is the most powerful power plant in Croatia with 486 MW capacity.", "The first phase of the hydroelectric plant was completed in 1961.", "It produces an average of 1,450 gigawatt-hours of electricity per year.", "The facility is an underground cavern type, built inside a mountain.", "It utilizes water from the Cetina River basin and Peruća reservoir.", "A full modernization of all four generating units was completed by 2017."],
